            0.182
          ],
          "content": "1. On a number line, draw lines of lengths $\\frac{1}{10}   \\text{; } \\frac{3}{10}$ , and $\\frac{4}{5}$ ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.189,
            0.839,
            0.238
          ],
          "content": "2. Write five more fractions of your choice and mark them on the number line."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.251,
            0.84,
            0.302
          ],
          "content": "3. \u0007How many fractions lie between 0 and 1? Think, discuss with your classmates, and write your answer."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.313,
            0.885,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": "4. What is the length of the blue line and black line shown below? The distance between 0 and 1 is 1 unit long, and it is divided into two equal parts. The length of each part is ${ \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } .$ . So the blue line $\\mathrm { i s } \\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ units long. Write the fraction that gives the length of the black line in the box."
        },
        {
